# iface_value_name_collision_factory.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): a private `codec::Reader` struct and a
# dynamic-dispatch `stream::Reader` interface share the SAME bare last segment (issue #109); a
# bare-`Reader`-typed method param must bind in its OWNER module's namespace, not whichever
# same-bare declaration the resolver happens to visit first. Flattening into one snippet would
# collide the two same-bare `Reader` types outright. Kept on disk, unflattened; not
# inline-scenario-izable.

#
# UNFOLD (2026-07-26, owner ruling "está proibido inline code em tkr"): this project is also a HOST
# for scenarios that used to be `Given source inline` blocks in regressor.tkr. Each is a MEMBER
# NAMESPACE under `src/`, selected by `TEKO_REGR_ENTRY`, and every one of them runs off THIS
# project's SINGLE build — the runner compiles a project's `.tkp` at most once per `.tkr`
# (`RegrBuilt`), and the members differ only by the env selector, args and stdin, never by source.
# The project's own scenario is unchanged and still runs from the same binary with no selector set.

Feature: iface_value_name_collision_factory — same-bare-name types across namespaces resolve in their own module

  Scenario: a bare-Reader-typed param binds to its OWN module's Reader, never the cross-namespace same-bare collider
    When built and run
    Then exit = 10

Feature: F3 null-union — scalar, struct, class shapes (unfolded from regressor.tkr — members of this project's single build)

  Scenario: struct Point | null, present and absent
    Given env = ["TEKO_REGR_ENTRY=q002_struct_point_null_present_and_absent"]
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42


